Rejected at Step 0; no generator was produced, as required when G/H/V cannot all be met.

Key findings from the [full paper](https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.09981):

- Track A fails: the paper proves existence, not hardness for a generated distribution.
- Track B fails: the natural line-graph family’s public compact route is the same as root reconstruction plus Euler traversal.
- A degree-aware greedy attack solved 20/20 theorem-regime instances at 246 vertices in median 0.024 seconds.
- The Section 2 sharpness construction is false as written for \(k\ge1\): an explicit spanning tree has only one branch vertex in its stem.

The complete evidence, measurements, mechanical/compact cost comparison, and counterexample are in [REJECTED.md](/home/gson/gvrepo/results/1802.09981/REJECTED.md).
